                <pb facs="0601" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 17172/2A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the King of Italy.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>With all my countrymen, I am appalled by the dreadful calamity which has befallen
                    your country. I offer my sincerest sympathy. American National Red Cross has
                    issued appeal for contributions for the sufferers and notified me that they will
                    immediately communicate with the Italian Red Cross.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Theodore
                    Roosevelt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
